  {
    "title": "How many replicas?",
    "body": "About 5% of reads must be fresh and go to the leader (step 5), so 8,000 − 400 = 7,600 reads per second go to replicas. Each replica must also apply all 800 writes per second it receives from the leader, so at the safe limit of 2,100 queries per second it has 2,100 − 800 = 1,300 left for reads. 7,600 ÷ 1,300 ≈ 5.8, so **6 replicas**. Replicas add read capacity only: if writes reached 2,100 per second, a replica would have no room left for reads.",
