  {
    "title": "Read your own writes",
    "body": "The fix is **read-your-writes**: after a customer changes something, their own reads of that data go to the **leader** for a short time, here 30 seconds. This works because the team takes any replica more than 10 seconds behind out of service, so no replica is ever more than 10 seconds old. Everyone else keeps reading from replicas. Another way is to remember the change's position in the log and only use a replica that has caught up to it.",
