  {
    "title": "The leader fails",
    "body": "The leader's server dies. In a **failover**, a follower is **promoted** to be the new leader, and the app server sends writes to it. With asynchronous replication, writes that reached the old leader but not yet the follower are gone: late in the evening, with a lag of 3 seconds at 200 writes per second, up to **600** writes that customers were told had succeeded. Promoting a synchronous follower instead would keep every confirmed write; promoting a lagging asynchronous one would not.",
