  {
    "title": "Replication is not a backup",
    "body": "An engineer deletes a day of orders by mistake. The leader applies the delete, and every replica copies it within a second. Only a **backup** kept separately can help: restore last night's full backup, then replay the archived log up to one minute before the delete (**point-in-time recovery**). That also removes the valid orders placed after the delete, so the team copies them back from the damaged database. The **RPO** says how much data may be lost and sets how often the log is archived; the **RTO** says how long recovery may take and must be checked by a real restore: 400 GB at 200 MB/s is about 33 minutes before the log replay.",
